        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A durable epoxy floor comes from doing the boring steps in the right order: test the slab two weeks ahead, degrease and grind on prep day, repair and vacuum thoroughly, then mix carefully and roll at the right temperature. The coating itself is the quickest part of the job.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If your slab fails the moisture test or you cannot spare the time for proper prep, a different floor may serve you better. If it passes and you follow the plan, even a modest kit can give you a clean, bright garage floor that lasts for years.
          </p>
